  "ams7902": {
    "id": "ams7902",
    "tag": "QUESTIONABLE",
    "what_was_obtained": "An AMS7902G file whose header says page 3 of 9 and whose pdfinfo reports 3 pages. Section 1.3 says there are three sheet and plate classifications based on flatness tolerances and points to 3.5.5. Section 3.5.5 is not in the file. Revision H was not opened.",
    "doi_current": "https://doi.org/10.4271/AMS7902H",
    "g_identity_read": {
      "revision": "G",
      "issued": "1961-07",
      "revised": "2015-01",
      "reaffirmed": "2018-12",
      "sheet_inch": [
        0.02,
        0.25
      ],
      "sheet_finish": "no greater than 55 Ra (63 microinches, 1.6 micrometres), ASME B46.1"
    },
    "class_tolerances_read": false,
    "note": "Sheet flatness, once the table is obtained, is a rolled-sheet allowance. It is not cell telegraphing of a bonded panel and not the wrinkle component. The 55 Ra figure is roughness, not delta. Lead faces 0.6917 mm and 0.8434 mm sit inside the sheet band. No class number is stated here."
  },
  "answer": {
    "cell_scale": "The only printed cell-scale depth, 0.001651 mm on an aluminum-foil coupon, is under every needed amplitude. The 3/8-inch cells in that report are slopes. A rise held at the larger slope across a whole cell is still under the smallest needed amplitude. That bound is a projection.",
    "short_wave_not_cell": "Leighton figures of 0.010 to 0.024 mm rms are under every needed amplitude as numbers, on scales longer than about 10 to 40 mm. They are not the wrinkle component, and the cell is inside the 10 mm average.",
    "whole_panel": "The 1969 honeycomb rms, 0.2032 mm from the printed 0.008 inch, is larger than every needed amplitude. It is a panel rms. Stock per-foot bows on the 032 card are the same kind of mismatch.",
    "exceeded_today": "Needed amplitudes are exceeded as numbers by whole-panel honeycomb rms and by per-foot shop bows. They are not exceeded by the cell-scale depth that was printed, nor by the Leighton rms on the scales that instrument measured. No page gives a beryllium face on CR-III 3/8-1.0 at the wrinkle wavelength.",
    "processes": [
      "1969 commercial honeycomb, Rohr figure via von Hoerner: panel rms above the needed amplitudes",
      "stock bonded panels, per-foot or per-metre bows already on the 032 card: above, wrong gauge length",
      "machined-core plus epoxied 1 mm aluminum sheet, Leighton: rms below, scales longer than a cell",
      "aluminum-foil vacuum-bag coupons, NASA ER-1001: cell dimple below"
    ]
  }
